
%% Response-injection router (A5 Stage B): the answer to an agent's own cold
%% call, injected into its input stream as response(Target, Response), the
%% agent called and its answer --- an alternative of the input message type in
%% its own right, never a msg(person, Id, ...), whose first argument is the
%% role tag.  Generalised over the injected value type R and the agent input
%% stream type S, both inferred at each call.  The clause constructs
%% response(_, _) into the S stream, so per-instantiation checking verifies
%% that S carries that shape at each instantiation.

exported procedure(R, S) inject_msg(R?, Key?, Stream(S)?, Stream(S)).
inject_msg(Resp, Target, Ys, [response(Target?, Resp?)|Ys?]) :-
    known(Resp?) | true.
inject_msg(Resp, Target, [Y|Ys], [Y?|Ys1?]) :-
    inject_msg(Resp?, Target?, Ys?, Ys1).
